# Captured evidence — byte-exact, never line-ending-normalized.
#
# `*` rather than a file list, deliberately. SHA256SUMS covers every file in
# this bundle including README.md and this file, so ANY path that escapes the
# pattern can be line-ending-normalized on checkout (core.autocrlf) and fail
# `sha256sum -c` on a bundle nobody tampered with — the exact false alarm this
# is here to prevent. A list has to be kept in sync with the bundle's contents;
# `*` cannot fall out of sync.
#
# Patterns are relative to the directory containing this file, so they must be
# bare globs — a path-prefixed pattern silently matches nothing. Verify with:
#   git check-attr text -- docs/evidence/<bundle>/<file>
# Expect `text: unset`. `text: unspecified` means the protection is inert.
* -text
